{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation","id":1426899,"title":"20th Anniversary Path of Transmutation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-01T19:57:53-08:00","id":1426899,"title":"20th Anniversary Path of Transmutation?","content":"This seems to be the one path I did not find from the old revised. Does it still exist in V20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T10:19:11-08:00","id":1426999,"title":"","content":"In fact, there are several such paths. Vine of Dionysus, Soul of the Serpent (quite a rare power, although it belongs to the Setites), Hearth Path and many others. On the other hand, the main task (of book) was to provide a set of everything necessary for a <b>standard</b> game. In order to write the history of each path, describe its powers, describe which sect this path belongs to - it takes time and <b><u>space</u></b>. V20 will be too big if someone fit everything from previous editions.<br /> <br /> I think there is nothing to be surprised if I say that all vamp-sorcerers have many rituals and paths that were not written in the book. Unique aztecs magic. Or assamite sumerian magic or time-travel rituals. Tremere have a ritual that forces all werewolves in a certain area to forcibly transform into wolfs &amp; etc.<br /> <br /> Just use &quot;lost paths&quot; from 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-02-2020, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:45:42-08:00","id":1427041,"title":"","content":"pretty sure they nuked it in V20, probably too strong for v20...but hey, you can still do Alchemy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (damn this emote is irritating)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:56:04-08:00","id":1427044,"title":"","content":"Maybe we should discuss gaol here?<br /> Let's discuss questions: is it necessary to balance this power? or how victim can potentially escape from it?<br /> <br /> Something like that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T15:33:21-08:00","id":1427048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation?p=1427044#post1427044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we should discuss gaol here?<br /> Let's discuss questions: is it necessary to balance this power? or how victim can potentially escape from it?<br /> <br /> Something like that...</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot the details of gaol,<br /> maybe they can escape with protean 5, obtenebration 5 or Vicissitude 5, maybe path of mercury as well, or movement of the mind (and transmutation of course),<br /> I imagine vampires would still be able to use Presence to make the blood mage cancel gaol,<br /> <br /> that's all I can think of as far as using it on vampires goes,<br /> if used on mortals and ghouls however...I don't see anyway out of it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T16:19:29-08:00","id":1427053,"title":"","content":"seems strange they would think that too much and have no worries about Focused Mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T04:08:37-08:00","id":1427123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain America</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation?p=1427053#post1427053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">seems strange they would think that too much and have no worries about Focused Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that path is broken. Seriously, why can't vampires enhance their brains with magic? <span style=\"font-size:10px\">In fact, in Dark Ages, while they were mortals, they had the opportunity to develop mental potential.</span><br /> Much more dangerous was path of Morpheus. Technically, it is still mentioned in the V20, however Morpheus top power was scary. (Perhaps worse than death in dream is sleep curse. I mean, someone can just curse a vampire and leave him somewhere to sleep until someone fulfills an unknown awakening condition.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Gaol is not so bad. It might even make sense, I mean, it would be a pretty weird air-prison if it broke down in a few turns. Although there is a feeling of a certain helplessness for a victim devoid of mystical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T04:45:15-08:00","id":1427124,"title":"","content":"I'd theorize that Focused Mind was kept because celerity and temporis were still a thing,<br /> plus they made celerity actions happen in the same turn as when the power is activated<br /> <br /> and transmutation kinda shits on any attempt at using mortals or ghouls as effective agents,<br /> on top of being &quot;Alchemy but easier&quot;<br /> <br /> anyway, imo they shouldn't have removed those paths, they should've just made them a bit easier to counter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T06:14:15-08:00","id":1427132,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think so. This path is about mind of thaumaturge. It was clearly created for &quot;mind&quot; activities.<br /> <br /> I don't think they &quot;removed&quot; most paths from 4ed (like old-disciplines kai &amp; maleficia). <i><span style=\"font-size:9px\">Its hard to write all known paths, elder disciplines, rituals, combodiscip, roads, etc. into the main book.</span></i> However, I do not understand the purpose of weakening magic to the point that ordinary ghoul will humiliate wizard who controls matter, wine or house (or transform into snakes). Then discipline will become useless with this tendency.<br /> <br /> What did you mean when you wrote about transmutation and agents? Did you mean that agents won't help trem with path? Or that ghouls can't be melted like iron club?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-03-2020, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:18:07-08:00","id":1427163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation?p=1427132#post1427132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did you mean when you wrote about transmutation and agents? Did you mean that agents won't help trem with path? Or that ghouls can't be melted like iron club?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that if you were the kind of vampire who relied on mortal agents to do the dirty work (like, say a Ventrue with mortal/ghoul bodyguards), those agents will be powerless against a blood mage with Transmutation<br /> <br /> Gaol would insta kill them and other transmutation powers can make them trip on the floor or find themselves falling from the 10th floor or something funny like that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t think so. This path is about mind of thaumaturge. It was clearly created for &quot;mind&quot; activities. </div> </div> </div>did I say the opposite?<br /> <br /> I meant to say that Focused mind allowed you to either counter celerity/Temporis or be on equal footing by allowing you to use magic a second time in one turn<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think they &quot;removed&quot; most paths from 4ed (like old-disciplines kai &amp; maleficia). <i><span style=\"font-size:9px\">Its hard to write all known paths, elder disciplines, rituals, combodiscip, roads, etc. into the main book.</span></i> However, I do not understand the purpose of weakening magic to the point that ordinary ghoul will humiliate wizard who controls matter, wine or house (or transform into snakes). Then discipline will become useless with this tendency. </div> </div> </div>in a way, they wanted ghouls to humiliate wizards,<br /> they wanted mortals to be a threat to vampires, as if they weren't enough of a threat during the day<br /> <br /> this probably won't change,<br /> they hired Justin Achilly for the next books,<br /> he's known to have made vampires weak in Revised, and he's the one who did Vampire the Requiem, where vampires were also weak<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T14:50:31-08:00","id":1427205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation?p=1427163#post1427163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> did I say the opposite?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You were hinting that this path was saved exclusively to counter Temporis / Celerity... or so I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T15:40:48-08:00","id":1427211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation?p=1427205#post1427205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You were hinting that this path was saved exclusively to counter Temporis / Celerity... or so I thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>if by &quot;saved&quot;, you mean &quot;not deleted&quot;, then no<br /> celerity is not the only reason the path was not deleted<br /> <br /> however, even if not &quot;deleted&quot;, a path can still be &quot;nerfed&quot;, as they did to spirit manipulation,<br /> and, in my speculation, the reason the path of focused mind wasn't nerfed was because of celerity<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T04:31:08-08:00","id":1427261,"title":"","content":"I didn't understand what happened to Spirit Manipulation. It looks like they left everything as it was (&amp; slightly changed the first 2 powers). Or am I missing something?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Perfect Clarity has a short duration (in combat), What else can we do there? <br /> Dual Thought, it works only for one turn. Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T07:46:53-08:00","id":1427271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation?p=1427261#post1427261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't understand what happened to Spirit Manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>they nerfed fetishes (spirit manipulation 4 iirc)<br /> you used to be able to make similar fetishes to the one Garou made,<br /> in v20, the fetishes are less interesting<br /> <br /> still, spirit manipulation is still good in v20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 12-04-2020, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T12:33:14-08:00","id":1427292,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Perfect Clarity, does the reduced -2 difficulty on roll actions also work for mental actions and by extension on mental disciplines like thaumaturgy ? Making this path the most coveted of all Tremeres. Not to mention the previous Levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25708-richard","name":"Richard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T12:59:52-08:00","id":1427293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426899-20th-anniversary-path-of-transmutation?p=1427271#post1427271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they nerfed fetishes (spirit manipulation 4 iirc)<br /> you used to be able to make similar fetishes to the one Garou made,<br /> in v20, the fetishes are less interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that in 3rd edition it was proposed to find werewolf book and take fetish rule for this. I think they are not EA to sell DLC-books to everyone who bought an add-on to main book.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>It's nice that Vampire let's you incorporate things from Wraith and Werewolf and etc without having to buy those books. But if you have access to them and they are going to feature in the game in a significant way, use those.</i></span> (-Mistocles)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll say one thing, I'm not <b>RAW </b>fanatic. PoSM in V20 is still good mostly because it hasn't been changed, except for fetishes.<br /> Here's what I think - V20 and RotB aren't perfect. These books tried to fit a lot of things, many of these things were later changed &amp; improved (in DAV20).<br /> You can recall that they removed (in RotB) all magic that does not use willpower. Unique magic of Setites? In trash. Unique elementalist magic of Slavs / Europeans? In trash. They <b>left </b>mentions that other (non-thaum) magic works <b>differently </b>and that book will not write this unique rules. This makes me think that previous editions are still useful, at least because there are lore and originality left there.<br /> They changed it (in DAV) for better, MotM became more useful than before, introduced unique botches for different paths. They improved Abyssal Mysticism, showed a unique discipline-magic (and removed addiction to Wits roll and unavoidable permanent side effects).<br /> <br /> What I mean by this is that we can go back to old fetishes rules (or even combine them). They tried to simplify everything so that we would not forced to buy (then not yet published books?) other books.<br /> <br /> <br /> About Perfect Clarity - yes. It makes sense, it says it affects all actions. I can also recall that the mind plays an important role in thaumaturgy (just some lore from old book and hermetism).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-04-2020, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}